{
  "evidence": "TEXT_D: Free personal care for elderly/disabled; free eye and dental checks; broader prescription exemptions; more clinicians and faster diagnosis; abolish tuition/top‑up fees and hire 21,000 teachers with smaller class sizes; Single Equality Act and hate‑crime units; 10,000 more police and a UK Border Force; ban smoking in enclosed public places; zero‑waste goal, 60% recycling, at least 20% electricity from renewables, precaution on GM, and strong animal welfare. Progressive taxation with a 50% rate above £100k and replacing Council Tax with a Local Income Tax based on ability to pay. TEXT_G: Near‑zero net immigration with strict controls; repeal the Human Rights Act; withdraw from the EU and reassert national control (e.g., fisheries); increase defense spending and tougher law‑and‑order measures; NHS decentralisation and extended GP hours; extensive deregulation including scrapping the Working Time Directive; restrict GM crop planting until long‑term safety is proven.",
  "reasoning": "Because Care is the highest‑priority foundation in the profile, TEXT_D’s extensive commitments to free personal care, expanded health services, education investment, and public‑health protections align more closely than TEXT_G’s deregulation and immigration‑first agenda. TEXT_D also provides adequate Authority (more police, Border Force) and Sanctity (public‑health and environmental prudence), whereas TEXT_G emphasizes Loyalty/Authority at the expense of Care and Equality, which are still meaningful in the profile.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_D"
}
